WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.930
- Well there's something
else that I thought

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:04.290
was kinda cool that you're doing.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.340
So you have, it's a new
line at Wal-Mart, right?

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.430
A new clothing line?

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.749
- Yeah, yeah.
- Talk to me about that.

00:00:09.749 --> 00:00:11.206
That's amazing, (talking over each other)

00:00:11.206 --> 00:00:12.400
that's a huge brand.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.950
- I know, you know, it's funny.

00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:19.750
When I was home, I drove by the Wal-Mart

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.630
that my mom and I had to walk to

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.370
because my mom's car didn't work.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.203
- Oh!

00:00:24.203 --> 00:00:25.380
- You know, and it was super far.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.510
I mean, it felt like 10 miles.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.490
I think it was only four, but regardless.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.017
I was like, "Oh my gosh,
I have this partnership

00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:32.437
"with a brand that I've been, you know,

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:34.410
"literally shopping at forever."

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:37.720
But when I was a young
kid, a chubby little girl,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.130
they didn't have cute clothes.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:42.723
There weren't cute girl
clothes for chubby girls.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.510
Or for anybody that was sort of outside

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.510
of a straight size, just generally.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:51.330
And now that they are
incorporating such incredible,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.690
it's affordable, but it's also trendy.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:54.760
And I think that's really important,

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:57.400
'cause I think when we
feel good, we do good

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.610
and all of that, it's
all sort of encompassing.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.840
And so when I was even
approached by Wal-Mart,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.407
I was like, "Oh well, yeah,
like this makes sense for me

00:01:06.407 --> 00:01:10.110
"because it's something
that I think is just..."

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.390
- I think it's real, that's what I like.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:13.230
It's believable, it's
like, I'm the same girl.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.830
I shopped there too, growing up.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.870
I think, you know, for some people,

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:19.287
they hear like, "Oh well you don't need

00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:20.710
"to be trendy, like that's not important."

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.280
It's like, you don't realize
how important that is

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.600
unless you don't fit in that circle.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.630
You don't realize how
devastating that is for a kid.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.740
You know, even me, I grew up,
you know, with Payless shoes

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:32.650
and everybody else had
Nikes and it was like,

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.590
my shoes were the ones
that made black marks

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:35.817
all over the basketball court.

00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:39.037
And those kind of things
count and that really does,

00:01:39.037 --> 00:01:42.300
you know, you start recognizing
your life and your being

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.460
as less than.
- Yeah.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.240
- And so I think that
it's really important

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.730
and awesome that they reached out to you

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.940
because you represent a lot
of the American community

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:51.010
and the world community.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.350
And so I think it's really important that

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.400
when any of us do these sponsored things

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.690
or these endorsements or these deals,

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.500
that it's believable and it's real.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.960
And that's what I really loved about it,

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.410
so thank you for doing it, it's cool.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.065
- Yeah, I'm super grateful
and it's funny how,

00:02:05.065 --> 00:02:09.116
you know, life happens and
how it all kind of pulls in.

00:02:09.116 --> 00:02:10.947
I'm like, "Oh, I would never
have thought, you know,

00:02:10.947 --> 00:02:13.367
"a girl struggling (chuckles)
in Gainesville, Florida would,

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.687
"you know, have sort of a really

00:02:14.687 --> 00:02:16.230
"important partnership with--"

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:18.340
- Yeah, and can create such an impact

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:20.150
for other little girls in Gainesville

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.566
that are going through the same thing, so.

00:02:21.566 --> 00:02:22.399
- Right!

00:02:22.399 --> 00:02:24.196
- I think that's the coolest
thing we're able to do

00:02:24.196 --> 00:02:26.170
with whatever you wanna call this,

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.425
our little version of superpowers, so.

00:02:28.425 --> 00:02:29.337
(laughing)

